<title>AUSTRIA: Austria cenbank sees 85 pct chance EMU on time.</title>
<headline>Austria cenbank sees 85 pct chance EMU on time.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian central bank chief Klaus Liebscher said in an interview published on Wednesday the probability of European monetary union (EMU) coming into effect on schedule in 1999 were 85 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;I would say: there is an 85 percent probability monetary union will start on time,&quot; Liebscher told weekly magazine Falter. &quot;I can't look into the future, that is why I would not say I am 100 percent convinced (that EMU will start on time).&quot;</p>
</text>
